│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compact_crx_ansatz                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The seed ansatz uses 24 parameters per block across three rotation layers (RY, RZ, RZ)    │
│                          │ and a linear CZ chain. While it achieves high accuracy (0.98), it is parameter-heavy (146 │
│                          │ total params), resulting in a lower parameter efficiency score.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I am proposing a more compact and expressive ansatz that reduces the parameters per block │
│                          │ from 24 to 16. This new design uses:                                                      │
│                          │ 1. A layer of RY rotations (8 parameters) for state preparation.                          │
│                          │ 2. A circular layer of parametrized CRX gates (8 parameters), which provide both          │
│                          │ entanglement and controlled X-rotations.                                                  │
│                          │ 3. A fixed circular CZ layer with a stride of 2 to ensure more global connectivity across │
│                          │ the 8-qubit register.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By reducing the parameters per block to 16, the total parameter count drops from 146 to   │
│                          │ 98 (16 params * 6 blocks + 2 calibration params). This significantly improves the         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency metric while the increased expressiveness of the CRX gates and       │
│                          │ circular connectivity aims to maintain or improve the classification accuracy.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
