│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz achieves excellent performance (0.98 test accuracy, 0.01               │
│                          │ generalization gap) but uses 146 total parameters across all blocks, resulting in         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency of only 0.01. The current ANSATZ_SPEC has 32 parameters per block (8 │
│                          │ independent RY + 8 independent RZ_pre + 8 independent RZ_post).                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements in the new design:                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter Sharing Strategy**: Instead of 32 independent parameters per block, reduce │
│                          │ to 10-12 by using:                                                                        │
│                          │    - 2 shared RY parameters applied in an alternating pattern (ry_a on qubits 0,2,4,6 and │
│                          │ ry_b on qubits 1,3,5,7)                                                                   │
│                          │    - Single shared RZ_pre parameter across all qubits                                     │
│                          │    - Single shared RZ_post parameter across all qubits                                    │
│                          │    - 2-3 parametrized CRZ gates for controlled local rotation (more expressive per        │
│                          │ parameter)                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Enhanced Connectivity**: Replace the simple line of CZ gates with a combination:     │
│                          │    - Parallel CZ pairs: [0,1], [2,3], [4,5], [6,7]                                        │
│                          │    - Cross-connections: [1,2], [3,4], [5,6], [7,0]                                        │
│                          │    - This provides better mixing while maintaining reasonable depth                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Parametrized Two-Qubit Gates**: Introduce 2-3 parametrized CRZ gates strategically   │
│                          │ placed to improve expressivity without many additional parameters (3 more parameters but  │
│                          │ significant expressivity gain).                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Reduce n_params from 146 to approximately 80-90 (about 40% reduction)                   │
│                          │ - Improve parameter_efficiency from 0.01 to ~0.011-0.012                                  │
│                          │ - Maintain or slightly improve test accuracy (currently at 0.98) through better gate      │
│                          │ selection                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Reduce circuit depth by using shared parameters                                         │
│                          │ - Keep generalization gap low through controlled complexity                               │
