│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the fully independent per-qubit rotation stack with a more regular,    │
│                          │ parameter-shared hardware-efficient block.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - It cuts circuit parameters from 24 per block to 8 per block, which should improve       │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and reduce overfitting.                                              │
│                          │ - It keeps each qubit active, so expressivity is still reasonable despite the reduction.  │
│                          │ - The two entangling CZ layers are staggered: first on local pairs, then on cross-ring    │
│                          │ pairs. This improves information flow across the 8-qubit register without adding          │
│                          │ controlled-rotation overhead.                                                             │
│                          │ - Using an RX layer after entanglement complements the initial RY layer and tends to      │
│                          │ improve amplitude mixing for Z-basis readout.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a strong regularized ansatz for a data-reuploading classifier: fewer     │
│                          │ trainable parameters, lower depth, and better inductive bias while preserving enough      │
│                          │ structure to fit the task.                                                                │
