│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_parity_compact                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the line-based, 8-parameter-per-layer pattern with a more compact      │
│                          │ ring-entangling block.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - The previous final RZ layer was mostly diagonal and therefore weakly effective against  │
│                          │ the fixed ZZ feature map and Z-basis readout.                                             │
│                          │ - A full CZ ring gives each qubit direct global mixing in one layer, which is a better    │
│                          │ fit for the re-uploaded feature map.                                                      │
│                          │ - Parity-shared RY/RX layers keep the block expressive while cutting the number of        │
│                          │ trainable circuit parameters per block from 8 to 4.                                       │
│                          │ - Fewer parameters should improve parameter efficiency and reduce overfitting, while      │
│                          │ keeping enough non-diagonal basis changes to preserve accuracy.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this keeps the architecture lightweight, more symmetric, and better aligned with │
│                          │ the fixed phase-encoding data pipeline.                                                   │
