│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate achieved a perfect 1.0 accuracy on both train and test sets but    │
│                          │ used 50 total parameters. To improve the `combined_score`, we can significantly increase  │
│                          │ the `parameter_efficiency` by reducing the number of unique parameters per block while    │
│                          │ maintaining the same expressive circuit structure.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I have updated the `ANSATZ_SPEC` to share parameters across qubits (even/odd wires)       │
│                          │ instead of more granular groups. This reduces the number of unique parameters per block   │
│                          │ from 8 to 4. With $l=3$ re-uploads and $p=2$ repeats, the total circuit parameters        │
│                          │ decrease from 48 to 24, bringing the total parameter count (including gain and bias) to   │
│                          │ 26. This increases the theoretical `parameter_efficiency` from 0.02 to approximately      │
│                          │ 0.038. I also maintained the periodic CZ ring structure and the alternating RY/RX layers, │
│                          │ which have already proven effective for this binary classification task.                  │
