│ patch_description        │ Replace the current RZ/CRZ-heavy block with a compact butterfly-style hardware-efficient  │
│                          │ ansatz.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Keeps the total trainable budget at 16 parameters per block, matching the previously    │
│                          │ strongest parameter regime.                                                               │
│                          │ - Removes redundant phase-only layers that add depth but little direct value for Z        │
│                          │ readout.                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Uses two noncommuting single-qubit layers (RY then RX) to convert the feature-map       │
│                          │ phases into measurable amplitude differences.                                             │
│                          │ - Uses two sparse CZ butterfly stages to spread information globally across the 8 qubits  │
│                          │ with lower depth than the current ring-plus-cross pattern.                                │
│                          │ - This should improve convergence speed, reduce gate count/depth, and preserve the strong │
│                          │ validation/test performance seen in the best prior runs.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a targeted efficiency upgrade: same parameter count class, better        │
│                          │ connectivity structure, and less circuit overhead.                                        │
