│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_mixed_axes                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a complex ansatz with many pre/post RZ layers and mixed CZ/CRZ   │
│                          │ gates, resulting in 158 parameters and 306 gates, with slower convergence (210 steps)     │
│                          │ than the previous best candidate (1.44 score, 150 steps).                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior best candidate (score 1.44) achieved perfect accuracy with only 98 parameters   │
│                          │ and 228 gates using a simpler ring topology of CRX gates plus RY rotations. The           │
│                          │ recommendation is to introduce axis diversity to the ring while maintaining the efficient │
│                          │ topology.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose implementing a **mixed-axis ring ansatz**: alternate between CRX and CRY gates  │
│                          │ on even/odd ring edges respectively. This:                                                │
│                          │ 1. Reduces from 158 to 98 parameters (same as best prior)                                 │
│                          │ 2. Reduces from 306 to 228 gates (same as best prior)                                     │
│                          │ 3. Introduces rotation-axis diversity on different ring edges (CRX on 0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7; │
│                          │ CRY on 1-2, 3-4, 5-6, 7-0)                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Maintains simple, efficient structure shown to converge quickly                        │
│                          │ 5. Increases expressivity through heterogeneous two-qubit rotations without parameter     │
│                          │ bloat                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The gate pattern provides structured axis variety without excessive parametrization,      │
│                          │ following the recommendation for axis diversity while respecting the efficient topology   │
│                          │ that achieved the best prior score.                                                       │
