│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ trainable_coupled_ansatz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses aggressive parameter sharing and only fixed entanglers, leading  │
│                          │ to poor expressiveness and slow convergence (750 steps vs. 150 in the best prior          │
│                          │ program). The key issues are:                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Excessive parameter sharing** reduces model capacity and forces single parameters to │
│                          │ represent diverse quantum interactions                                                    │
│                          │ 2. **Fixed entanglers only** (all CZ) prevent the optimizer from tuning interaction       │
│                          │ strengths                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. **Insufficient trainable two-qubit gates** limit the ability to learn long-range       │
│                          │ correlations                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior best program (score 1.44) achieved 100% accuracy with 98 parameters by:         │
│                          │ - Using independent single-qubit RY rotations (no sharing)                                │
│                          │ - Including a ring of trainable CRX gates                                                 │
│                          │ - Keeping fixed CZ for rapid structure                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed improvement balances expressiveness and efficiency:                          │
│                          │ - **Replace fixed CZ gates with trainable CRZ gates**: This adds ~4-8 trainable           │
│                          │ parameters per block for direct coupling strength tuning                                  │
│                          │ - **Independent single-qubit rotations (RY + RZ)**: Removes parameter sharing to allow    │
│                          │ per-qubit customization                                                                   │
│                          │ - **Hybrid entanglement pattern**: Combines independent CRX pairs with trainable CRZ      │
│                          │ pairs for multi-scale interactions                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This aims to achieve ~120-140 circuit parameters (more than current 50, but close to the  │
│                          │ efficient best-prior 98) while dramatically improving convergence speed and validation    │
│                          │ accuracy through better parameterization.                                                 │
