│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 1.41) underperforms compared to prior implementations (scores  │
│                          │ 1.44–1.45). The primary issue is its ansatz structure: while achieving 100% accuracy and  │
│                          │ low depth, it produces higher validation/test loss (0.09 vs 0.03–0.05).                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis shows that the second prior program (score 1.45) uses alternating CRX and CRY    │
│                          │ parametrized gates in a ring topology with fixed CZ gates, achieving better validation    │
│                          │ loss (0.03) despite identical parameter count and similar gate count.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Replace the current ansatz with the alternating CRX/CRY ring structure from the        │
│                          │ high-performing second program                                                            │
│                          │ 2. This structure provides better expressivity for the classification task by:            │
│                          │    - Using both X and Y controlled rotations alternately around the qubit ring            │
│                          │    - Maintaining systematic two-qubit coupling with fixed CZ gates                        │
│                          │    - Creating a more balanced parametrization landscape                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ANSATZ_SPEC directly incorporates the proven topology (8 RY rotations +           │
│                          │ alternating CRX/CRY around the ring + two layers of CZ couplings), which empirically      │
│                          │ reduced validation loss from 0.09 to 0.03 while maintaining 100% accuracy.                │
