│ patch_description        │ This design draws inspiration from the strong performance of the prior programs while     │
│                          │ implementing a fundamentally novel approach to parameterized two-qubit gates.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights from prior context:                                                          │
│                          │ 1. The second program achieved perfect validation/test accuracy (1.00) using all-CRX      │
│                          │ parameterized gates with a ring topology, showing that controlled rotations are highly    │
│                          │ effective.                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. The current program alternates between CRX and CRY gates, achieving similarly strong   │
│                          │ results (0.99 validation, 1.00 test).                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Both top performers use 16 parameters per ansatz block with a ring-like qubit          │
│                          │ connectivity pattern.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach:                                                                           │
│                          │ Rather than using a single type (CRX) or pairs (CRX/CRY), this design rotates through ALL │
│                          │ three parameterized controlled rotation types (CRX → CRY → CRZ → CRX...) around the ring. │
│                          │ This creates a richer expressivity landscape where each type of controlled rotation       │
│                          │ operates on different pairs, potentially:                                                 │
│                          │ - Enabling better feature encoding with diverse rotation axes                             │
│                          │ - Improving gradient flow through heterogeneous parameterization                          │
│                          │ - Reducing training plateaus by avoiding repetitive gate patterns                         │
│                          │ - Maintaining the efficient ring connectivity that proved successful                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fixed CZ offset gates remain unchanged, preserving the established global             │
│                          │ entanglement structure. Single-qubit RY rotations stay consistent. This mixing of CRX,    │
│                          │ CRY, and CRZ in sequence should maintain parameter efficiency (16 params/block × 3        │
│                          │ uploads × 2 repeats = 98 total) while potentially improving convergence dynamics and      │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
