│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ promote_cz_to_crz_remove_rz_post                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program performs significantly worse (1.26 vs 1.45) despite having MORE       │
│                          │ parameters (146 vs 98). This indicates overparameterization and poor parameter            │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Prior top performers used 98 parameters: 8 RY + 8 CRX/CRY ring + 8 fixed CZ gates = 16  │
│                          │ params/block × 6 blocks                                                                   │
│                          │ - Current uses 146 parameters: adds 8 RZ post-gates, bringing to 24 params/block × 6      │
│                          │ blocks                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Despite 50% more parameters, accuracy dropped from 1.00 to 0.98 and loss increased      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The redundant RZ post-gates appear to hurt generalization without providing benefit.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. **Remove the 8 RZ post-gates** to eliminate overparameterization (return to 16         │
│                          │ params/block baseline)                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. **Convert fixed CZ gates to trainable CRZ gates** with unique parameters (adds back 8  │
│                          │ params/block = 24 total, same as current but higher quality)                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the alternating CRX/CRY ring pattern from top-performing prior program     │
│                          │ while replacing ineffective RZ post-gates with trainable long-range phase couplings. CRZ  │
│                          │ gates directly control entanglement strength, complementing the fixed IsingZZ feature     │
│                          │ map's phase encoding. This should improve optimization landscape and decision boundary    │
│                          │ tightness.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Net effect: Maintain reasonable parameter count (~114 total) but with better-quality      │
│                          │ gates, restoring accuracy toward 1.45+ level.                                             │
